  <div id="sutta">
  
            <h4 id="thag1.119" class="h1">Thag 1:119  Vajjiputta</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>Coming to the bower</p>
              <p>at the root of a tree,</p>
              <p>placing</p>
              <p class="v2">unbinding</p>
              <p>in your heart,</p>
              <p>do jhāna, Gotama,</p>
              <p>&amp; don’t be heedless.</p>
              <p class="v1">What use is this</p>
              <p class="v1">chitter-chatter</p>
              <p class="v1">to you?<span class="fn"><a href="#thag1.119note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
            </div><!--end verse-->
            <div class="note">
              <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
              <p id="thag1.119note01">1. In SN 9:5, a deva addresses this verse to Ven. Ānanda, who has been spending too much time teaching Dhamma to laypeople.</p>
            </div><!--end notes-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
